      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Chylothorax is a rare but serious complication of cardiac surgery, with a poor prognosis unless treated properly. We report the case of 66-year-old woman who developed chylothorax after coronary artery bypass grafting. The chylothorax was successfully treated in 8 days by means of subcutaneous octreotide administration and a diet that contained medium-chain triglycerides. Octreotide, a long-acting somatostatin analog, is an effective and safe agent for the treatment of postoperative chylothorax and may reduce the need for reoperation."},
